sections.text:
Given a failure, T outputs a candidate note n as structured JSON rather than a worked example. Each note is an abstract, reusable rule intended for retrieval on future tasks with similar structure:

• note_key: unique identifier (reused when updating an existing rule);

• trigger_pattern: task features that should activate the note;

• corrective_rule: an executable fix directive for S;

• minimal_steps: a short ordered checklist lowering interpretation cost for a weak LLM;

• tags: domain or skill labels for routing;

• quality_score: initial confidence, later updated from validation statistics.

Notes deliberately avoid storing full solutions to x; they compress failures into transferable guardrails. Granularity and wording are calibrated to the student agent's capability.
